  46:     - Blue bars are markers; red bars are body bars that may be chained after a marker.
  47:     Rule
  48:     - Starting at each blue bar, repeatedly include the next red bar whose column is exactly the current bar's column plus the current bar's height.
  49:     - Clear every included vertical bar, then redraw each included bar horizontally to the right from its original bottom cell, with length equal to its vertical height.
  50:     - Red bars that are not reached from a blue marker remain unchanged.
  51:     Key insight
  52:     - A vertical bar's height is also the width it occupies after rotation, so the chain follows immediate horizontal contact after each rotated bar.
  53:     """
